> Converted from personal notes. Amounts are for one serving. Directions are editorial, not verified source instructions.

> REVIEW: Range 1/5 to 2/5: upper amount 2/5 selected for shopping.

> Additional source: https://mykoreankitchen.com/wprm_print/spicy-gochujang-mayo

== Ingredients ==

Gather the following ingredients: @thinly sliced ribeye or sirloin{3/10%lb}, @dry jasmine rice{3/10%cup}, @gluten-free tamari{1/20%cup}, @brown sugar{2/5%tbsp}, @honey{1/5%tbsp}, @grated Asian pear or apple{1/15%cup}, @garlic cloves{4/5} (minced), @grated ginger{1/5%tbsp}, @sesame oil{2/5%tsp}, @rice vinegar{1/5%tbsp}, @green onions{3/5} (sliced), @sesame seeds{1/5%tbsp}, @gluten-free mayo{1/10%cup}, @gluten-free gochujang{2/5%tbsp}, @lime juice{1/5%tbsp}, @water{2/5%tbsp} (to thin).

== Preparation ==

Cook rice separately. Marinate thinly sliced beef with tamari, sugar, honey, grated fruit, garlic, ginger, sesame oil and vinegar. Sear in batches. Mix mayonnaise, gochujang and lime, thinning with water as needed. Serve with rice, green onion and sesame.
